 blood of whom, having his marrow pierced (by me) and slain by me in battle, dose the Earth wish to drink?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.614,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-19-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3018006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"356b075c65362964b621360f41efdafb942f6ed07ec332ee9918330d7e365e77","compact":"1ea37cf436d8fb14eb80ba2dedeea9d4bb7ba4553c8114fa5efe948a2de6e9aa","nasal":"1ea37cf436d8fb14eb80ba2dedeea9d4bb7ba4553c8114fa5efe948a2de6e9aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-18-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":18,"verse":7,"english":"Tearing off flesh from the corpse of whom slain by me in conflict, shall the birds so joyfully feed on it?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-19-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3018007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0520d86672b5e6bc0fa50d981af3ca2f2615a70eb1654e7bcc4209e8949fe27","compact":"97f727a9e9618b4438ce96f4ded2ae717d637cbefa31aae9b7dde06bb8a8064c","nasal":"adc5ee01a96abeef043f075fe7ce2a4258995fdb4aca26cce7dc46db655d5e50"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-18-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":18,"verse":8,"english":"Him, whom I shall wrong mightily, neither the gods, nor the Gandharvas, nor the Piśācas, nor the Rākşasas, will be able to rescue in fierce encounter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-19-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3018008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cbfb9f21d5e591accf136d8272f77485e65d5ca31fabf34446eb830729dbe522","compact":"adfb3cd13ce48d4aa5e79ac33aa93c7ee43f2a31327007345c4ec81d95fd8240","nasal":"ee7bd011f4a02267bbbf12ba098a786305f8d33bc7cca3b1dfaf5b4e12a89456"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-18-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":18,"verse":9,"english":"Recovering by degrees your sense, it behoves you to tell me what individual it was of execrable character, who by his prowess, half humbled you in the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-19-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3018009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f9bac96032bab8dd4d6b9bfcb1833253714fefea8000b3ad9a06ea4489f2afbc","compact":"f014d91c162b9707116773b01823dddb52d89e63051f0723e4ce7723204e197f","nasal":"f014d91c162b9707116773b01823dddb52d89e63051f0723e4ce7723204e197f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-18-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":18,"verse":10,"english":"Hearing these words of his brother, who was under the influence of extreme rage, Sūrpanakhā with tears in her eyes, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-19-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3018010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8aee8b8739fb41fa3629dfe083ae7903cbb3aa4439f8910262911ad163290000","compact":"39a4285444345cb9bfa119c4e386abee4ff13af237255b2d3b4302896d39afc3","nasal":"39a4285444345cb9bfa119c4e386abee4ff13af237255b2d3b4302896d39afc3"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-18-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":18,"verse":11,"english":"Tender, and endowed with beauty, possessed of youth and gifted with great strength, with expansive eyes resembling white lotuses; clad in bark and dark dear-skins subsisting on fruits and roots, having their senses under control; leading an ascetic life and a Brahmacarya mode of existence; there are two sons of Dasaratha the brothers Räma and Lakşmaņa resembling the Sovereign of the Gandharvas, and marked with signs betokening royalty. I cannot ascertain whether they be celestial, or human beings.","alig